# This directory is the one place in the repo that OTHER PROGRAMS write into.
# Claude Code drops per-machine permission overrides here the first time you approve
# something permanently; plugins drop settings and session state beside them. None of
# that is the OS, and some of it names your machine, your paths, or your session ids.
#
# So the rule is a WHITELIST, not a blacklist. A blacklist has to predict what the next
# tool will leave behind, and the cost of guessing wrong is committing it — to a repo
# whose whole point is being forkable and published from. A whitelist's cost of guessing
# wrong is the opposite: something legitimate is silently NOT committed, and works
# locally forever (ledger L008 — the safe default for personal data is the silent
# default for generic code).
#
# Both halves are covered. The patterns below admit the SHAPES the OS ships, so a new
# hook or a new skill is tracked without anyone remembering to come back here. And
# tools/check-coverage.sh walks this directory and refuses anything that is neither
# tracked nor declared on the LOCAL_ONLY line, so a new KIND of file forces a decision
# instead of vanishing.

# Ignore everything...
*
# ...but descend into directories, or nothing below them could be re-admitted.
!*/

# ...then re-admit exactly what ships.
!.gitignore
!README.md
!settings.json
!hooks/*.sh
!skills/**

# ...except OS cruft, which `!skills/**` would otherwise re-admit. A later pattern wins,
# so this has to sit AFTER the whitelist, not with the ignores at the top.
.DS_Store

# Ignored on purpose. check-coverage.sh reads this line: a file under .claude/ that is
# neither tracked nor covered here is reported, rather than quietly left behind.
#
# It lists only what EVERY install sees. A GUI wrapper or editor plugin drops its own
# settings and session files here under its own name; add that name when it appears. Being
# reported once is not the mechanism failing, it is the mechanism asking, and answering it
# by name is cheaper than a pattern that would also swallow the next thing.
# LOCAL_ONLY: settings.local.json sessions .DS_Store
